m_EP2.7x2.7mm","pinout":false},"buy":[{"store":"LCSC","url":"https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2054058.html","priceUsd":2.66},{"store":"DigiKey","url":"https://www.digikey.com/en/products/result?keywords=XMC1100Q024F0064ABXUMA1"},{"store":"Mouser","url":"https://www.mouser.com/c/?q=XMC1100Q024F0064ABXUMA1"},{"store":"JLCPCB parts","url":"https://jlcpcb.com/parts/componentSearch?searchTxt=C2054058"},{"store":"Octopart","url":"https://octopart.com/search?q=XMC1100Q024F0064ABXUMA1"}]}],"released":2013,"status":"active","datasheetUrl":"https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-xmc1100_AB-DS-v01_08-EN.pdf?fileId=5546d4624a0bf290014a4bdaff9325bd","productUrl":"https://www.infineon.com/products/microcontroller/32bit-industrial-arm-cortex-m/xmc1000-m0/xmc1100","notes":["There are two USIC channels (USIC0 CH0/CH1). Each one is UART, SPI (also dual/quad SPI), I2C, I2S or LIN, so the uart/i2c/spi/i2s counts share the same 2 channels.","The CPU runs at 32 MHz while peripherals (PCLK) can run at 64 MHz. There is no FPU, MATH coprocessor, CAN, USB or DAC (those come with XMC1300/1400).","Only one CCU4 timer unit, so there are just 4 PWM outputs. LED/touch (LEDTS), BCCU and CCU8 are on XMC1200/1300, not the XMC1100.","ADC: 12 channels on TSSOP-38/VQFN-40, 8 on VQFN-24 and 6 on TSSOP-16. On TSSOP-38, 8 of the 34 port pins (P2.2-P2.9) are input-only analog/digital.","Devices ship in ASC (UART) bootstrap-loader mode via USIC0. Code is loaded to SRAM, so flashing needs a loader tool (e.g. XMC Flasher/DAVE), and the Boot Mode Index (BMI) must then be switched to a user mode. SWD or single-pin SPD debug works too.","The 128/200 KB versions (XMC1100-T038X0128/X0200) exist but are rarely stocked. flashKB reflects the 64 KB parts listed.","deepSleepUa is the datasheet deep-sleep figure (0.24 mA at 5 V, flash off). There is no hibernate mode, so this is not a coin-cell part.","USIC quad-SPI is a protocol mode, not a memory-mapped flash interface, so qspi is false.","Arduino support is the XMC-for-Arduino core (KIT_XMC11_BOOT_001 board); the PlatformIO platform is Infineon's infineonxmc."],"sources":["https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-xmc1100_AB-DS-v01_08-EN.pdf?fileId=5546d4624a0bf290014a4bdaff9325bd","https://www.infineon.com/dgdl/Infineon-xmc1100-AB_rm-UM-v01_03-EN.pdf?fileId=5546d46249cd1014014a0a8438a65e29","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C126702.html","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2054462.html","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C2054058.html","https://www.findchips.com/search/XMC1100T038F0064","https://github.com/Infineon/XMC-for-Arduino","https://github.com/Infineon/platformio-infineonxmc"],"boards":[]}